  "slides": [
    {
      "page_title": "What Compose Actually Is",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. Compose, Precisely",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "A spec + CLI turning one YAML into Docker API calls",
            "It creates networks, volumes and containers — that is all",
            "Not a runtime, not an orchestrator; the daemon still runs things",
            "Declarative with reconciliation: `up` diffs desired vs running",
            "Only changed image/env/ports/mounts get recreated"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "yaml",
          "lines": [
            "services:              # only required key",
            "  web:",
            "    image: nginx",
            "    ports: [\"8080:80\"]  # 3 lines = valid"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. The Project Namespaces Everything",
          "ink": "black"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Project name defaults to the directory name",
            "Project `shop` gives container `shop-web-1`",
            "…and network `shop_default`, volume `shop_db_data`",
            "Rename the folder and your volumes are orphaned"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Pin it via",
            "Form"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "CLI flag",
              "`-p myproj`"
            ],
            [
              "Env",
              "`COMPOSE_PROJECT_NAME`"
            ],
            [
              "YAML",
              "top-level `name:`"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. V1 Is EOL",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "",
            "V1",
            "V2"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Invoke",
              "`docker-compose`",
              "`docker compose`"
            ],
            [
              "Built in",
              "Python, dead",
              "Go plugin"
            ],
            [
              "Naming",
              "`proj_web_1`",
              "`proj-web-1`"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Delete `version:`",
          "text": "Obsolete in the Compose Specification. V2 ignores it and warns at every run."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Top-Level Keys",
          "ink": "black"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`services:` is the only required top key",
            "`networks:`, `volumes:`, `configs:`, `secrets:` are optional",
            "Declare shared resources there, reference them per service"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. Commands To Memorise",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Command",
            "Effect"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`up -d`",
              "create + start"
            ],
            [
              "`down` / `down -v`",
              "remove; `-v` kills volumes"
            ],
            [
              "`ps` / `logs -f`",
              "what runs / why it died"
            ],
            [
              "`exec` / `run --rm`",
              "attach / one-off container"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "`config` Is The Debugger",
          "text": "`docker compose config` prints the fully merged, variable-interpolated YAML Compose will actually act on."
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "yaml",
          "lines": [
            "build:",
            "  context: .",
            "  dockerfile: Dockerfile.api",
            "  target: prod        # multi-stage stage",
            "  cache_from: [app:latest]"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Service Keys: Command, Ports, Restart",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "6. A Service Is A Template",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "One definition, N containers — `scale` multiplies it",
            "`image:` pulls prebuilt; `build:` builds a Dockerfile",
            "Both together: build, then tag the result as `image:`",
            "Build `args` are build-time only, never in container env"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. command vs entrypoint",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`command:` overrides the image's CMD",
            "`entrypoint:` overrides ENTRYPOINT",
            "Setting `entrypoint:` resets CMD to empty — silent breakage",
            "Then supply the command back yourself"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "yaml",
          "lines": [
            "entrypoint: [\"/tini\", \"--\"]  # wipes CMD",
            "command: [\"node\", \"server.js\"]  # restore"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Ports Are For The Host",
          "ink": "black"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Short form is `HOST:CONTAINER` — `\"8080:80\"`",
            "`expose:` is documentation; does nothing on user-defined networks",
            "Internal-only services need no `ports:` at all"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "cloud",
          "title": "Quote Every Mapping",
          "text": "Unquoted `56:56` is YAML sexagesimal and becomes `3416`. Quoting is the whole fix."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. restart: Policies",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Policy",
            "Behaviour"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`no`",
              "default, never"
            ],
            [
              "`on-failure[:N]`",
              "nonzero exit, N tries"
            ],
            [
              "`always`",
              "also on daemon boot"
            ],
            [
              "`unless-stopped`",
              "not if you stopped it"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Runtime Knobs",
          "ink": "black"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`working_dir`, `user: \"1000:1000\"`, `hostname`",
            "`init: true` adds a PID 1 reaper for zombie processes",
            "`stop_grace_period: 30s`, `stop_signal: SIGINT`"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. profiles: Optional Tooling",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "yaml",
          "lines": [
            "debugger:",
            "  image: pgadmin",
            "  profiles: [\"debug\"]  # skipped by up",
            "# docker compose --profile debug up"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "6. deploy: Is Mostly Swarm",
          "ink": "black"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Key",
            "In Compose V2"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`resources.limits`",
              "honored (cpus, memory)"
            ],
            [
              "`replicas`",
              "honored"
            ],
            [
              "most other keys",
              "silently ignored"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "8. Long Form Fixes It",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "yaml",
          "lines": [
            "web:",
            "  depends_on:",
            "    db:",
            "      condition: service_healthy"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "depends_on and Start Ordering",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "7. depends_on Says 'Started'",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Short form guarantees start order, nothing more",
            "It never asks whether Postgres accepts connections",
            "App boots in 300ms, DB takes 8s, app dies: connection refused",
            "depends_on kept its promise; you still lost"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Condition",
            "Means"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`service_started`",
              "default, weak"
            ],
            [
              "`service_healthy`",
              "needs a healthcheck"
            ],
            [
              "`service_completed_successfully`",
              "exited 0"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`required: false` (2.20+) makes a missing dep non-fatal",
            "Shutdown follows the reverse order",
            "Transitive: `up web` starts the whole graph",
            "Circular deps are a hard parse-time error"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "yaml",
          "lines": [
            "migrate:                  # db: healthy",
            "  depends_on: {db: {condition: service_healthy}}",
            "web:                      # migrate: exited 0",
            "  depends_on:",
            "    migrate: {condition: service_completed_successfully}"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. Where depends_on Stops",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "No effect across separate Compose projects",
            "`docker compose run` starts deps by default; `--no-deps` skips",
            "It is a boot-time guarantee, never a mid-life one"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Belt And Braces",
          "text": "Healthcheck conditions in Compose plus connection retries in the app. Compose covers boot; retries cover the 3am restart."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. How Health Is Measured",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "A command run inside the container on an interval",
            "Exit 0 = healthy, exit 1 = unhealthy",
            "Docker stores the state; Compose only reads it"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "yaml",
          "lines": [
            "healthcheck:",
            "  test: [\"CMD-SHELL\", \"pg_isready -U app\"]",
            "  interval: 5s",
            "  retries: 5",
            "  start_period: 30s   # grace window"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`start_period` is essential for JVM and database boots",
            "`start_interval` marks a 2s-ready container healthy in 2s",
            "Without it you wait a full 30s interval for nothing"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Healthcheck Timers and Traps",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Two Forms Of test",
          "ink": "black"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Form",
            "Runs as",
            "Gets"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`CMD`",
              "exec, no shell",
              "no pipes, no `$VAR`"
            ],
            [
              "`CMD-SHELL`",
              "`/bin/sh -c`",
              "pipes, `||`, `$VAR`"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. The Five Timers",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Key",
            "Default",
            "Meaning"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`interval`",
              "30s",
              "gap between checks"
            ],
            [
              "`timeout`",
              "30s",
              "one check's budget"
            ],
            [
              "`retries`",
              "3",
              "fails before unhealthy"
            ],
            [
              "`start_period`",
              "0s",
              "failures don't count"
            ],
            [
              "`start_interval`",
              "—",
              "fast poll during start (25.0+)"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. States",
          "ink": "black"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              "starting",
              "healthy",
              "unhealthy"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "No healthcheck = no status reported at all",
            "`condition: service_healthy` on such a service fails immediately"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Detection Math",
          "text": "Worst case to notice failure ≈ interval × retries + timeout. Tune the numbers; never inherit the defaults blindly."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "6. Traps That Bite",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`curl` is absent from alpine and distroless images",
            "Use `wget --spider -q`, the runtime, or a static binary",
            "`test: [\"NONE\"]` disables an inherited check; `disable: true` too",
            "1s interval × 20 replicas = 20 process spawns per second",
            "Docker never restarts an unhealthy container by itself"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "cloud",
          "title": "restart ≠ health",
          "text": "`restart: always` reacts to process exits, not to health status. Only Swarm and Kubernetes act on health."
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "yaml",
          "lines": [
            "ports: [\"15432:5432\"]   # host only",
            "# from web:  postgres://db:5432/app",
            "# NOT db:15432 — host map is irrelevant"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Networks and DNS Discovery",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. One Network By Default",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Compose creates `<project>_default`, driver `bridge`",
            "Every service is attached to it automatically",
            "Declaring any `networks:` on a service replaces that attachment",
            "Forget to list `default` and the service loses its neighbours"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Discovery Is DNS",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Docker's embedded resolver sits at 127.0.0.11",
            "A service name resolves to its container IP",
            "`http://db:5432` just works — no links, no hardcoded IPs",
            "`aliases` add extra DNS names per network"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Container Port, Always",
          "text": "Internal traffic uses the container port. `ports:` exists only for host access — publishing an internal service is needless exposure."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Segmenting Tiers",
          "ink": "black"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "yaml",
          "lines": [
            "web:  {networks: [frontend]}",
            "api:  {networks: [frontend, backend]}",
            "db:   {networks: [backend]}",
            "networks:",
            "  backend: {internal: true}  # no egress"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`web` now physically cannot reach `db`",
            "`internal: true` blocks all outbound external routing",
            "That is the standard hardening for a database tier",
            "`external: true` joins a network Compose didn't create"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Scaled Names Resolve Wide",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "One name, multiple A records, returned in rotation",
            "That is crude round-robin with no proxy needed",
            "But clients cache resolutions and connections are sticky",
            "Dead replicas stay in DNS until the container is removed"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "cloud",
          "title": "Not Load Balancing",
          "text": "DNS rotation distributes lookups, not load. Put a real proxy in front when balance matters."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. host Mode Escape Hatch",
          "ink": "black"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`network_mode: host` skips the network namespace (Linux only)",
            "Ports bind directly on the host",
            "`networks:` alongside it is illegal"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "yaml",
          "lines": [
            "volumes:",
            "  - db_data:/var/lib/postgresql/data  # named",
            "  - ./src:/app/src                    # bind",
            "volumes:",
            "  db_data:            # top-level decl"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Volumes: Mount Types and Shadowing",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "6. Three Mount Types",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Type",
            "Lives in",
            "Survives"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "named volume",
              "`/var/lib/docker/volumes`",
              "yes"
            ],
            [
              "bind mount",
              "a host path",
              "host's problem"
            ],
            [
              "tmpfs",
              "RAM",
              "no, gone on stop"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. Naming And Ownership",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Named volumes become `<project>_db_data`",
            "A bind mount is any path with `/` or `.`",
            "`external: true` points at an outside volume",
            "External volumes are exempt from `down -v`"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "yaml",
          "lines": [
            "- type: volume        # long syntax",
            "  source: db_data",
            "  target: /var/lib/postgresql/data",
            "  read_only: false"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. The Key Asymmetry",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "An empty named volume is pre-populated from the image path",
            "A bind mount never is — it shadows what the image had",
            "That is the `node_modules` disappearing act",
            "`./:/app` hides the installed modules entirely"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "yaml",
          "lines": [
            "volumes:",
            "  - ./:/app             # shadows image",
            "  - /app/node_modules   # anon vol on top"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Permissions And Speed",
          "ink": "black"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Bind mounts inherit host permissions verbatim",
            "UID 1000 writing a root-owned host dir gets EACCES",
            "Mismatched UIDs are the #1 volume bug",
            "Docker Desktop binds cross a VM boundary — slow for many files",
            "Named volumes stay inside the VM and are fast"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Flag",
            "Use"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`:ro`",
              "config, certs"
            ],
            [
              "`:z` / `:Z`",
              "SELinux relabel (RHEL)"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Deletion Rules",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`down` keeps named volumes",
            "`down -v` deletes them, with no undo",
            "`docker volume prune` clears anonymous and unused ones",
            "`volumes_from` is deprecated — share a named volume instead"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Pick By Purpose",
          "text": "Named volumes for state, bind mounts for dev source, tmpfs for secrets and scratch."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Env Vars: Interpolation and Precedence",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. Two Different Env Worlds",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Shapes",
            "Source",
            "Seen by"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "the YAML",
              "shell + `.env`",
              "Compose parser"
            ],
            [
              "the container",
              "`environment:` / `env_file:`",
              "your process"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "6. Interpolation Defaults",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Form",
            "Fires when"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`${VAR:-def}`",
              "unset or empty"
            ],
            [
              "`${VAR-def}`",
              "unset only"
            ],
            [
              "`${VAR:?msg}`",
              "fails loudly"
            ],
            [
              "`$$`",
              "literal `$`"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`${VAR}` is substituted at parse time, before Docker sees anything",
            "`environment:`/`env_file:` are invisible to YAML interpolation",
            "`.env` is auto-loaded from the project dir (or `--env-file`)",
            "`.env` feeds interpolation only — it does not populate containers"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "yaml",
          "lines": [
            "# .env:  TAG=1.4.2",
            "image: app:${TAG:-latest}",
            "environment:",
            "  DSN: pg://db/${DB_NAME:?set it}"
          ],
          "note": "substituted before Docker sees it"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. Writing environment:",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "yaml",
          "lines": [
            "environment:",
            "  LOG_LEVEL: debug     # map form",
            "  - API_KEY=abc123     # list form",
            "  - HOME               # pass through host"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Bare `- KEY` with no `=` inherits from the host shell",
            "`env_file:` takes a list; later files win",
            "Since 2.24: `{ path: ..., required: false }`"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Precedence, Highest First",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`docker compose run -e`",
            "shell environment (pass-through keys)",
            "`environment:`",
            "`env_file:`",
            "Dockerfile `ENV`"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "cloud",
          "title": "env_file Is Not Shell",
          "text": "No `export`, no command substitution. Quotes are handled by Compose's own parser, not bash."
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Escape With `$$`",
          "text": "A literal `$` in a password or `command:` must be written `$$`, or Compose eats it as a variable and leaves an empty string."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Secrets Belong In Files",
          "ink": "black"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Secrets, Override Files and Merge Rules",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Never commit real credentials to `.env`",
            "Gitignore it and ship a `.env.example`",
            "`secrets:` mounts files under `/run/secrets/`",
            "Env vars leak into `docker inspect`, `config`, child processes",
            "File-based secrets do not"
          ]
